    "text": "The radii of two planets are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and their densities are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;represent the acceleration due to gravity at their respective surfaces, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is",
